  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 216 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe threat for dangerous heat stress conditions into at least \nmidweek remains our message this weekend. Upper-level ridge shifting \nwestward across the region is the primary driver of current very hot \nair temperatures. 850mb temperatures of 20-23 C are supporting \ndaytime max temps near 100 with deep mixing in our region. The \nhumidity is lessened by mixing as well, but still enough to keep \ndaily heat index values maxing out around 105-115 degrees. A Heat \nAdvisory remains in place for the next few days. Some portions of \nthe area could exceed 110 degree heat indices tomorrow, and a \nportion of the area may need to be upgraded to an Excessive Heat \nWarning.\n\nBy midweek, the ridge will consolidate and amplify over the Desert \nSouthwest, letting a trough pattern set up over the eastern CONUS. \nThere should be relief from the heat at least in the form of \n\"cooler\" air behind a cold front, but rain chances will increase \nalong and ahead of the cold front passage. Thursday onward, most \nlocations have at least a slight chance for showers or \nthunderstorms. /NF/",
